        "t": "chr",
        "v": [
          "This module assesses whether the paper's code could be run on its data, and — because `execute = TRUE` — **actually ran it**. We examined 2 R code files.",
          "#### Run order",
          "The scripts were ordered by their data dependencies (a script writing a file another reads runs first), `source()` calls, and numeric filename prefixes.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Order = 1:2, File = c(\"01_prep.R\", \"02_analysis.R\"\n), \"Runs after\" = c(\"—\", \"01_prep.R\"), Basis = c(\"numeric\", \n\"dependency\")), row.names = c(NA, -2L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### File paths",
          "Every data path in the code works in the repository as deposited.",
          "#### Files the deposit does not hold",
          "The scripts that did not run through read 1 data file that is not in the deposit, and no script of the deposit writes: `not_shared.csv`.",
          "#### Execution",
          "**The code was run.** Each script ran in an isolated subprocess against a throwaway copy of the repository, in the run order above, with a 60-second per-script timeout. Of 2 scripts: 1 ran without error, 1 errored, 0 timed out, 0 could not run because one of its own dependencies is unavailable, 0 did not parse. Running against current package versions: a break can reflect version drift, which argues for pinning versions. **1 script stopped on a file another script writes**, so it was run once more after the other scripts: `02_analysis.R` (clean_data.csv). One file was written in another folder than where the script looked, so before that run we copied it there: `clean_data.csv` to `code/clean_data.csv` for `02_analysis.R`. The scripts assume they all run from one folder; saying which, or building paths from the top of the project (as with `here::here()`), solves this. Which script must run first can be stated in a README, or shown by numbering the file names (01_, 02_).",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = c(\"01_prep.R\", \"02_analysis.R\"), Outcome = c(\"ran_ok\", \n\"errored\"), Detail = c(\"\", \"runtime\"), \"Time (s)\" = 0), row.names = c(NA, -2L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 15, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "*Expand a row below to see the output each script produced.*",
          "::: {.callout-tip title=\"Output — 01_prep.R (ran_ok)\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n**Output (stdout):**\n````\n> raw <- read.csv(\"data/raw_data.csv\")\n> clean <- raw[!is.na(raw$score), ]\n> write.csv(clean, \"clean_data.csv\", row.names = FALSE)\n````\n\n:::\n",
          "::: {.callout-tip title=\"Output — 02_analysis.R (errored)\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n**Output (stdout):**\n````\n> library(stats)\n> dat <- read.csv(\"clean_data.csv\")\n> t.test(score ~ group, data = dat)\n\n\tWelch Two Sample t-test\n\ndata:  score by group\nt = -3.4125, df = 3.999, p-value = 0.02698\nalternative hypothesis: true difference in means between group a and group b is not equal to 0\n95 percent confidence interval:\n -2.2973452 -0.2359881\nsample estimates:\nmean in group a mean in group b \n       3.300000        4.566667 \n\n> missing <- read.csv(\"not_shared.csv\")\n````\n**Messages / errors (stderr):**\n````\nError in file(file, \"rt\") : cannot open the connection\nIn addition: Warning message:\nIn file(file, \"rt\") :\n  cannot open file 'not_shared.csv': No such file or directory\n````\n\n:::\n"
